        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "An exclusive coastal residence perched in an elevated position, commanding uninterrupted panoramic sea views. The property offers flexible accommodation, complemented by a beautifully appointed one-bedroom self-contained annexe.\r\n\r\nThis exceptional residence offers a rare opportunity to enjoy coastal living in one of West Cork’s most scenic locations. Step outside for a swim in the sheltered cove, enjoy walks along the coastline, or simply relax and take in the uninterrupted panoramic views across the Ocean and the rugged coastline towards the Seven Heads Peninsula.\r\n\r\nThe property which extends to 122.23 sq. m (1,315 sq. ft) is set on approximately one-third of an acre of private grounds with a mature garden, a workshop, bike shed and a one-bedroom self-contained annexe.\r\n\r\nMain House\r\nThe accommodation is designed to make the most of the property’s spectacular setting. A welcoming open porch leads to a bright triple-aspect entrance hall, which opens onto a sunny terrace.\r\n\r\nThe open-plan kitchen, dining and living area is the heart of the home, with floor-to-ceiling glazing and sliding doors framing the coastal views and providing direct access to the garden.\r\n\r\nThe principal bedroom is generously proportioned and benefits from an en-suite shower room and access to the rear terrace. A second spacious double bedroom enjoys large windows and sliding doors overlooking the front of the property, making the most of the panoramic views. A family bathroom completes the accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe house is presented in excellent condition throughout, with bright, well-proportioned rooms and an abundance of natural light.\r\n\r\nSelf Contained 1 Bedroom Annexe\r\nThe attached one-bedroom annexe  has its own independent entrance.\r\n\r\nIt is ideal for guest accommodation, independent accommodation for a family member or a supplementary income.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises an open-plan kitchen, dining and living area with large windows and sliding doors overlooking the coast, together with a double bedroom and bathroom. It is presented in excellent condition throughout.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nThere is ample private parking to the front of the property and along the driveway. The mature tiered gardens provide attractive outdoor spaces ideal for entertaining and relaxing, while a workshop offers excellent space for hobbies and a separate bike shed provides practical storage.\r\n\r\nDunnycove is a peaceful secluded coastal enclave on the West Cork shoreline away from the busier coastal routes. The sheltered cove is perfect for swimming, paddle boarding, kayaking and boating.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nThe property has a lovely private situation  yet is very convenient to access. It is only 10 minutes to Clonakilty and the N71 National Road which connects Cork City with Bandon, Clonakilty and all the way west to Kenmare in Co. Kerry.\r\n\r\nCork International Airport is 55 minutes away and Cork City Centre 1 hour.\r\n\r\nThe vibrant heritage town of Clonakilty is renowned for its welcoming community and excellent range of amenities, including schools, healthcare services, supermarkets, boutique shops, cafés, award-winning restaurants, hotels and a wealth of independent local businesses.\r\n\r\nThe surrounding coastline is one of West Cork’s greatest attractions, with numerous beautiful beaches and scenic destinations close by, including Dunnycove, Dunneen Beach, Red Strand, Inchydoney, Long Strand, Owenahincha, The Warren, Blind Strand, Broadstrand and the wonderful walking trails through Castlefreke Woods to name a few.\r\n\r\nThe Mountain House Pub is only a few minutes drive away. It is a beautiful traditional pub and restaurant serving locally sourced food and drink. The restaurant has an award winning chef.\r\n\r\nFeatures–\r\n\r\nMains Water supply\r\n\r\nPrivate Septic Tank\r\n\r\nElectric and solid fuel heating system\r\n\r\nGas connection for the Cooker\r\n\r\nChrome Heated Towel Rails\r\n\r\nElectric Power Showers\r\n\r\nKinetic lighting system to external steps\r\n\r\nExternal Electricity points and Water Tap at parking area\r\n\r\nEircode: P85 VW92(Property Specific Code)\r\n\r\nViewing Is Highly Recommended – Strictly By Appointment Only\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDisclaimer: All information provided is to the best of our knowledge but is not guaranteed and should be independently verified. No warranties or representations are made regarding the accuracy, completeness, condition or planning status of the property. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of all information provided, including measurements, boundaries, size or acreage, BER details and services. All measurements and distances are approximate and for guidance only. Photographs and video are for illustrative purposes and may include items not included in the sale (e.g. furniture)."
